statement:
Retain one common canonical small-defect intact instance of accepted facts 0636caea9cc33c59, 592d2827cca44396, 624b3258dee4faea, 6496cb3b0fd44f9d, 6769574fc1bd9f8d, and 6bfe50fed9a5540b.  Use the notation of 0636caea9cc33c59 and 592d2827cca44396, and abbreviate
\[
 P:=P_{\mathrm{all}},
 \qquad
 \alpha:=\alpha_{\mathrm{all}}=\frac{P}{\Omega_b},
 \qquad
 \delta_0:=\frac{95}{97}
 \left(\frac{3\log(4/3)}{\log2}-1\right)>0.
\tag{1}
\]
Thus
\[
 0<\alpha\leq\frac14,
 \qquad
 P>\frac Q{24},
 \qquad
 \Omega_b>\frac{97}{100}Q.
\tag{2}
\]
The fresh gauge-load-minimal KKT optimizer for the matching capacity \(b\) is decomposed into its nonzero support-minimal packets as
\[
 v_k^b=\sum_r v_k^{(r)},
 \qquad
 v_k^{(r)}=\omega_k^{(r)}a_k^\circ,
 \qquad
 \sum_r\omega_k^{(r)}=\omega_k^b,
\tag{3}
\]
where, whenever \(\omega_k^b>0\),
\[
 a_k^\circ:=\frac{v_k^b}{\omega_k^b},
 \qquad
 h_{D_k}(a_k^\circ)=1.
\tag{4}
\]
For every packet put
\[
 \Omega_r:=\sum_k\omega_k^{(r)}>0,
 \qquad
 c_k^{(r)}:=\alpha\omega_k^{(r)},
 \qquad
 C_r:=\sum_kc_k^{(r)}=\alpha\Omega_r.
\tag{5}
\]
Then
\[
 \sum_k\omega_k^{(r)}a_k^\circ=0,
 \qquad
 \sum_k\omega_k^{(r)}a_k^\circ m_k^{\mathsf T}=0,
 \qquad
 \sum_r\Omega_r=\Omega_b,
\tag{6}
\]
and
\[
 \sum_r C_r=P,
 \qquad
 \alpha\Delta_C(b)=\sum_r\delta_r>\delta_0P,
\tag{7}
\]
where \(\delta_r=-\sum_k h_{L_k}(\alpha v_k^{(r)})>0\).

For every positive fresh edge \(k\), retain the canonical objects
\[
 m_k\in\mathbb Z^n,
 \qquad
 L_k=\overline c_k+D_k
 \subseteq\mathsf M_{\vartheta_k}(C_{m_k}),
\tag{8}
\]
and the one physical target ledger
\[
 \boxed{
 \sum_{k:m_k=m}\frac{\omega_k^b}{\vartheta_k}\leq1
 \qquad(m\in\mathbb Z^n).}
\tag{9}
\]
For every triple \((r,i,k)\) with \(\omega_i^{(r)}\omega_k^{(r)}>0\), choose
\[
 p_{i\mid k}^{(r)}\in F_{L_k}(a_i^\circ)
 :=\{p\in L_k:\langle a_i^\circ,p\rangle=h_{L_k}(a_i^\circ)\}.
\tag{10}
\]
For every \(i\) with \(\omega_i^b>0\), also choose one own support contact
\[
 q_i^{\mathrm{sup}}\in F_{L_i}(a_i^\circ).
\tag{11}
\]
Define the unscaled packet product coupling
\[
 \boxed{
 B_{i,k}^{(r)}
 :=\frac{\omega_i^{(r)}\omega_k^{(r)}}{\Omega_r}.}
\tag{12}
\]
It has the exact marginals
\[
 \boxed{
 \sum_iB_{i,k}^{(r)}=\omega_k^{(r)},
 \qquad
 \sum_kB_{i,k}^{(r)}=\omega_i^{(r)},
 \qquad
 \sum_{r,i}B_{i,k}^{(r)}=\omega_k^b.}
\tag{13}
\]
In particular, its physical target use is exactly
\[
 \boxed{
 \sum_{\substack{r,i,k\\m_k=m}}
 \frac{B_{i,k}^{(r)}}{\vartheta_k}
 =\sum_{k:m_k=m}\frac{\omega_k^b}{\vartheta_k}
 \leq1.}
\tag{14}
\]
Moreover, every packet-target block is zero-force:
\[
 \boxed{
 \sum_iB_{i,k}^{(r)}a_i^\circ=0.}
\tag{15}
\]
Consequently
\[
 \sum_{r,i,k}B_{i,k}^{(r)}a_i^\circ=0,
 \qquad
 \sum_{r,i,k}B_{i,k}^{(r)}a_i^\circ m_k^{\mathsf T}=0.
\tag{16}
\]

Put
\[
 \boxed{
 \nu_{\mathrm{full}}
 :=\gamma_d\sum_{r,i,k}B_{i,k}^{(r)}
 \delta_{(m_k,p_{i\mid k}^{(r)})},
 \qquad
 \gamma_d:=\left(\frac d{d+1}\right)^d.}
\tag{17}
\]
This is one collision-pooled physical measure.  Every closed ambient halfspace \(H\) satisfies
\[
 \boxed{\nu_{\mathrm{full}}(H)\leq\mu_C(H),}
\tag{18}
\]
and
\[
 \boxed{
 |\nu_{\mathrm{full}}|
 =\gamma_d\Omega_b
 >\frac{97\gamma_d}{100}Q.}
\tag{19}
\]

Define the all-packet cross-gauge energy and cross-work by
\[
 \mathcal E_{\mathrm{full}}
 :=\sum_{r,i,k}B_{i,k}^{(r)}h_{D_k}(a_i^\circ),
\tag{20}
\]
\[
 \mathcal T_{\mathrm{full}}
 :=\sum_{r,i,k}B_{i,k}^{(r)}
 \left\langle a_i^\circ,
 p_{i\mid k}^{(r)}-q_i^{\mathrm{sup}}\right\rangle.
\tag{21}
\]
Then
\[
 \boxed{
 \mathcal E_{\mathrm{full}}\geq0,
 \qquad
 \mathcal T_{\mathrm{full}}
 =\mathcal E_{\mathrm{full}}+\Delta_C(b)
 >\delta_0\Omega_b.}
\tag{22}
\]
Thus no packet defect is lost in forming the single physical cloud.

The canonical scaled coupling is
\[
 \widetilde B_{i,k}^{(r)}
 :=\alpha B_{i,k}^{(r)}
 =\frac{c_i^{(r)}c_k^{(r)}}{C_r}.
\tag{23}
\]
The scaled measure \(\widetilde\nu_{\mathrm{full}}:=\alpha\nu_{\mathrm{full}}\) is still halfspace-dominated by \(\mu_C\), has mass \(\gamma_dP\), and its scaled work obeys
\[
 \boxed{
 \widetilde{\mathcal T}_{\mathrm{full}}
 :=\alpha\mathcal T_{\mathrm{full}}
 =\alpha\mathcal E_{\mathrm{full}}+\alpha\Delta_C(b)
 >\delta_0P.}
\tag{24}
\]

Retain the circuit-attachment data of 592d2827cca44396:
\[
 c_k:=\alpha\omega_k^b,
 \qquad
 \theta_k:=
 \begin{cases}
 \zeta_k'/c_k,&c_k>0,\\
 0,&c_k=0,
 \end{cases}
\tag{25}
\]
\[
 \kappa_k^{(r)}:=\theta_kc_k^{(r)},
 \qquad
 \varepsilon_k^{(r)}:=c_k^{(r)}-\kappa_k^{(r)}.
\tag{26}
\]
Then the scaled product has the exact nonnegative decomposition
\[
 \boxed{
 \widetilde B_{i,k}^{(r)}
 =B_{i,k}^{\mathrm{att},(r)}
 +B_{i,k}^{\mathrm{rem},(r)},}
\tag{27}
\]
where
\[
 B_{i,k}^{\mathrm{att},(r)}
 :=\frac{c_i^{(r)}}{C_r}\kappa_k^{(r)},
 \qquad
 B_{i,k}^{\mathrm{rem},(r)}
 :=\frac{c_i^{(r)}}{C_r}\varepsilon_k^{(r)}.
\tag{28}
\]
Their exact total masses and edge marginals are
\[
 \boxed{
 \sum_{r,i,k}B_{i,k}^{\mathrm{att},(r)}=P'>\frac{93}{97}P,
 \qquad
 \sum_{r,i,k}B_{i,k}^{\mathrm{rem},(r)}=P-P'<\frac4{97}P,}
\tag{29}
\]
\[
 \boxed{
 \sum_{r,i}B_{i,k}^{\mathrm{att},(r)}=\zeta_k',
 \qquad
 \sum_{r,i}B_{i,k}^{\mathrm{rem},(r)}=c_k-\zeta_k'.}
\tag{30}
\]
Both pieces separately retain packet-target zero force:
\[
 \sum_iB_{i,k}^{\mathrm{att},(r)}a_i^\circ=0,
 \qquad
 \sum_iB_{i,k}^{\mathrm{rem},(r)}a_i^\circ=0.
\tag{31}
\]

Finally, the entire attached part in (28) has an exact genuine four-point-circuit ancestry.  Let \(\mathcal G\) be the full circuit multigraph of 592d2827cca44396.  Its edge
\[
 e=(\sigma,g,h,r,s)
\tag{32}
\]
has weight \(x_e:=x_{\sigma,g,h}^{r,s}>0\), two separately counted endpoint slots \((r,g)\) and \((s,h)\), and the unchanged actual points
\[
 K_g,K_h,J_e^0,J_e^1
 \in C\cap(\mathbb Z^n\times\mathbb R^d),
 \qquad
 K_g+K_h=J_e^0+J_e^1.
\tag{33}
\]
For every such edge and packet indices \(i,j\), put
\[
 \boxed{
 y_{e,i,j}
 :=x_e\frac{c_i^{(r)}}{C_r}
          \frac{c_j^{(s)}}{C_s}.}
\tag{34}
\]
For a loop, the two factors refer to the two separately counted endpoint slots.  Then
\[
 \boxed{\sum_{i,j}y_{e,i,j}=x_e.}
\tag{35}
\]
For every fixed \((r,k,i)\), the sum of the contributions in (34) from first slots equal to \((r,k)\) and second slots equal to \((r,k)\) is exactly
\[
 \boxed{B_{i,k}^{\mathrm{att},(r)}.}
\tag{36}
\]
A loop whose two endpoint slots both equal \((r,k)\) contributes once through each orientation.  Consequently each positive \(y_{e,i,j}\) can label, without changing its weight, the two attached cross-contact atoms at those two slots while retaining the genuine circuit (33), and summing all decorations recovers both the attached cross-contact family and the original circuit family exactly.  In particular, the attached cross-contact target marginal is \(\zeta_k'\), while the decorated circuit family is only a nonnegative splitting of the already collision-safe family.  The ancestry marking is not an additional copy of either source or target capacity.

No assertion is made that the attached part alone carries a fixed fraction of the work in (24), or that cross-contact atoms are themselves circuit corners.  The exact work belongs to the full scaled product, while more than \(93/97\) of its mass has the circuit ancestry (32)--(36).  No terminal absorption inequality and no global Steiner-selector midpoint skeleton are asserted.
